- **Routing**: fully healthy — OSPF adjacencies are all FULL, every router and switch has correct routes to `10.200.0.0/24`, `10.1.1.0/24`, and `10.2.1.0/24`
- **Server processes**: Apache running on all web servers; `named` running on `dns_server`
- **IP connectivity**: hosts can ping every server and `curl http://10.200.0.3/` returns correct HTML — the data plane is intact
- **DNS zone**: `db.local` is valid — `web0.local` → 10.200.0.3, `web1.local` → 10.200.0.4, etc.
- **DNS resolution for `web0.local`**: succeeds (`dig @10.200.0.2 web0.local A` → `10.200.0.3`)
- **DNS resolution for bare `web0`**: returns **REFUSED** — `named` has `recursion no` and is only authoritative for the `local` zone; a bare-name query (`web0.`) has no zone match
- **`/etc/resolv.conf` on both hosts**: only `nameserver 10.200.0.2` — **`search local` is absent**

